hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1305","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Al-Nufaili told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad told us, Yazid bin Khusayfa told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman. Ibn Thawban, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you see someone selling or buying in the mosque, So say: May God not make you profit in your business, and if you see someone seeking something lost in it, say: May God not make you profitable.” Abu Bakr said: If the sale had not been concluded, it would not have happened, due to his saying, may God bless him and grant him peace: “By God, I will not make your business profitable.” Meaning"
